\beatat sets the duration(s) for a beat.
It must be included inside a bar definition,
otherwise it will throw an error.
Its syntax is the following:

\beatat 4

or

\beatat 4. 4

Multiple arguments can set different durations
for the beat of the sequencer. The line above
concerns a 5/8 bar, where the first beat lasts
three eighth notes and the second beat lasts
two eight notes.

When a beat duration is set, it is held for all
bars defined after it, until a new beat duration
is set.
For this reason, when setting a new beat duration,
it should be set at the beginning of the bar,
like the example below.

\bar beatat-1 {
    \beatat 4
    \inst c'4 cis'8 c' b4
}
